  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_041: multiprofile, pca_n2000, vit_l, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.6352) establishes a strong baseline. We have clear evidence that PCA outperforms scgpt (0.5232 vs 0.4214 in singleprofile), but scvi_n200 has never been tested in any multimodal setting. Config_049 changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while holding all other settings at their best-known values (multiprofile, vit_l, avgpool, weighted). This single-variable test directly answers whether a learned variational RNA encoder can capture complementary signal beyond PCA's linear dimensionality reduction. If scvi_n200 improves performance, it opens a new promising axis; if it underperforms, it confirms PCA is sufficient and redirects budget toward other unexplored dimensions. This is more informative than completing the aggregation×fusion 2×2 (config_047), where the avgpool>transformer gap (0.6287 vs 0.5988) is already large and the marginal information gain would be small."
}

